    <File_Area_Observational>
        <File>
            <file_name>0299171308_charon_cube.fit</file_name>
            <comment>
                This file contains only the spectral cube array with a minimal FITS header.
                
                Note that no display orientation information was supplied in any of the labels
                of the PDS3 files comprising this product. Since they were all produced by the
                ISIS3 software, the orientation is presumably the same in all cases.
            </comment>
        </File>
        
        <Header>
            <offset unit="byte">0</offset>
            <object_length unit="byte">2880</object_length>
            <parsing_standard_id>FITS 3.0</parsing_standard_id>
        </Header>
        
        <Array_3D_Spectrum>
            <local_identifier>SpectralCube</local_identifier>
            <offset unit="byte">2880</offset>
            <axes>3</axes>
            <axis_index_order>Last Index Fastest</axis_index_order>
            <description>
                Note that the PDS3 label included a series of hexidecimal codes
                to represent the various Special_Constants. The bit strings varied
                only by a single bit, and the bit string listed as being the 
                "CORE_VALID_MINIMUM" was a NaN encoding, which is nonsensical.
                A sample file was inspected, and only a single flag value was
                discovered. This value is indicated below as a general-purpose
                "missing" flag.
            </description>
            <Element_Array>
                <data_type>IEEE754LSBSingle</data_type>
                <unit>W/m**2/sr/μm</unit>
            </Element_Array>
            <Axis_Array>
                <axis_name>Band</axis_name>
                <elements>256</elements>
                <sequence_number>1</sequence_number>
            </Axis_Array>
            <Axis_Array>
                <axis_name>Line</axis_name>
                <elements>320</elements>
                <sequence_number>2</sequence_number>
            </Axis_Array>
            <Axis_Array>
                <axis_name>Sample</axis_name>
                <elements>320</elements>
                <sequence_number>3</sequence_number>
            </Axis_Array>
            <Special_Constants>
                <missing_constant>0xFF7FFFFF</missing_constant>
            </Special_Constants>
        </Array_3D_Spectrum>
    </File_Area_Observational>
    
